Chamfers and fillets: a contact along the edge of a face beyond that the
blend meets at an acute angle (mitcad#300).

ChFi3d_ContactsAlongFaceEdges puts a contact that runs along an edge E of
its face onto the face beyond E (Fv), with a transition on Fv. It took the
side of the contact where the blend lies as the side toward the other
contact, projected onto Fv: outside Fv where the blend meets Fv at an
obtuse angle. A convex edge chamfered as far as the edges of both its faces
where one meets the face beyond at a right angle (the lip of an opening, a
narrow upper opening over a wider pocket: the lip's inner wall and its
underside both vanish; a tab as wide and as high as its edge's chamfer)
gives an acute angle: the chamfer folds back under Fv, the other contact
lies under Fv's material, and Fv got a transition into itself (an invalid
shape of 18 faces where 23 were due). The side outside Fv is now taken
from E's direction in Fv (Fv lies on the left of its edges about its
parametric normal).

Upstream: new.
